course: dictionary
lesson: 2209
title: Country: a land, the countryside, or its people
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word country has more than one meaning, so use the words around it to choose the right one. Read the whole sentence and ask: does this sentence talk about a land, the fields outside town, or the people?
explain: «Canada is a big country.» Here country means a land with its own government, borders and people. Try swapping in land: «Canada is a big land» still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
explain: «We went to the country for the weekend.» Here the country means the countryside: farms and fields away from the towns. «The whole country watched the final.» Here it means the people of the nation. Each time, the clues tell you which meaning to use.
fact: A country is a land with its own government, borders and people.
fact: «The country» can mean the countryside, the farms and fields outside towns.
fact: «The whole country» can mean all the people of a nation.
fact: The UK has four countries: England, Scotland, Wales and Northern Ireland.
fact: «Big countries were not born big»: many countries have grown or changed over time, so their borders are not always the same.
exercise: «Canada is a big country.» What does country mean here? | A kind of music from the southern USA | *A land with its own government and borders | A field where farmers grow wheat | The sea beyond the coast
exercise: Dad says, «We went to the country for the weekend.» What does the country mean? | The people of a nation | A land with its own government | *The countryside, with farms and fields | The busy city centre
exercise: «The whole country watched the final.» What does the country mean here? | *The people of the nation | A type of music | A border with another land | The farms and fields outside town
test: Which word means the countryside, with farms and fields outside towns? | A flag | A border | The capital | *The country
test: «Big countries were not born big.» What does this sentence tell us? | Countries have no borders | Countries only exist on maps | *Countries can grow and change over time | Countries are always the same size
exam: Which of these is one of the four countries of the UK? | Paris | Texas | Canada | *Wales
